      <h2>2. Privacy, Anonymity and 1v1 Chat</h2>

      <p>Privacy is one of the most important considerations when choosing an online chat service, but privacy and anonymity are not identical.</p>

      <h3>2.1 What Does Anonymous Chat Mean?</h3>

      <p>Anonymous chat generally means that participants do not have to reveal their real-world identity to each other. Depending on the service, users may not need a public username, profile or personal biography.</p>

      <p>However, anonymity between users does not necessarily mean that the platform itself cannot process technical information.</p>

      <h3>2.2 What Does Private Chat Mean?</h3>

      <p>A private conversation usually means that the conversation is limited to specific participants rather than being visible to a public audience.</p>

      <p>Users should still check the platform's privacy policy to understand what information may be processed by the service.</p>

      <h3>2.3 Why the Difference Matters</h3>

      <p>A service can provide a private two-person conversation while still processing information required to operate the connection, prevent abuse, provide analytics or comply with legal obligations.</p>

      <p>For this reason, avoid assuming that “no profile” means “no data.” The privacy policy is the better source for understanding a platform's actual data practices.</p>

